UID:95009-1790879400-1790884800@bangaloreinternationalcentre.org
SUMMARY:The Four Billion Year Old Story of Consciousness
DESCRIPTION: \nWe tend to think of humans as special because of our superior intelligence\, a story that runs from spotting poisonous berries to Descartes’ I think\, therefore I am\, and now\, to the machines we worry will out-think us. This conversation asks a different question: was cognition ever really what made us human\, or is that just the story intelligence tells about itself? \nThe deeper question addressed is not how we came to think\, but rather how we came to cooperate. In ancient times\, capabilities were shared across a group: one read the stars\, another tracked prey. Cognition was distributed\, and cooperation was mutually beneficial. This discussion argues that perhaps\, intelligence did not come first. Perhaps\, consciousness evolved less to help us think\, and more to help us stay together. \nIn collaboration with:\n \nVenue: Seminar Halls\n\n\nCooperation\, Consciousness and What Makes Us Human\nRSVPs closed. Thank you for your interest.\n*Speakers*: Ramanan Laxminarayan\, Rohini Nilekani\n*Event Categories*: Books\, Health & Wellness\, Nonfiction\, Philosophy\, Society
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/the-four-billion-year-old-story-of-consciousness/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Books,Health & Wellness,Nonfiction,Philosophy,Society
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnail-2-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
