SUMMARY:Gandhi’s Long Shadow
DESCRIPTION: \nGandhi’s ideas did not go unchallenged\, even by those closest to his moment in history. This talk draws on the book Arguments with Gandhi\, examining the ideological disagreements he had with Marxists\, religious fundamentalists\, economic modernizers\, and anti-caste radicals. What can a century of disagreement teach us about how to live now? \nUsing Gandhi’s legacy as a lens\, the talk offers a moral and political history of the modern world\, one built as much from argument as from agreement. Gandhi’s debates with his contemporaries\, and later generations’ arguments with him\, foreground questions we have yet to resolve: how do we resist political tyranny? How do we address discrimination based on caste\, gender\, and race? And how do we achieve freedom from poverty without destroying the planet along the way? \nIn collaboration with: \n      \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nDebates about Nonviolence\, Justice\, Faith\, and Progress\nRSVPs closed for the Auditorium. RSVP for the Simulcast in Halls 1/2 here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdGGpR48j9yDEb7pbNwqoBaE9E-VylP0xRBvd-07-Mipf-StA/viewform?usp=pp_url).\n*Speaker*: Ramachandra Guha\n*Event Categories*: Books\, History\, Nonfiction\, Society
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/gandhis-long-shadow/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Books,History,Nonfiction,Society
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnail_GLS.jpg
