SUMMARY:Threads of Tradition
DESCRIPTION:Learn to adorn by hand\, one mirror and one stitch at a time! \nThis hands-on workshop introduces the Lambadi tradition of mirror embroidery\, an art that transforms fabric into a shimmering record of beauty\, heritage\, and pride. Participants will learn to attach mirrors to cloth using traditional stitches and motifs\, guided directly by artisans of the Porgai Artisans Association from Sittilingi Valley\, Tamil Nadu. \nTraditionally practiced by Lambadi women to mark textiles with identity and status\, this embroidery has been preserved across generations. The workshop is open to complete beginners and welcomes anyone curious about craft\, culture\, or new ways to personalize a garment. All materials are provided\, and those who wish to embellish a piece of their own are welcome to bring it along. \nIn Collaboration with: \n \nVenue: Board Room\n\n\nMirror Embroidery with Lambadi Artisans\nRSVPs closed. Thank you for your interest.\n*Facilitators*: Lalitha & Lambadi Artisans\n*Event Categories*: Heritage\, Textiles\, Workshops
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/threads-of-tradition/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Heritage,Textiles,Workshops
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnail_TOT.jpg
END:VEVENT
