SUMMARY:Svara Darshan
DESCRIPTION:\nThis morning concert offers an intimate encounter with the world of Hindustani music. Moving between traditional and contemporary compositions\, musicians draw on the rich heritage as it continues to blossom. Older bandish carry the imprint of the musicians who shaped them\, while newer compositions reveal a tradition still very much alive\, still evolving in real time. \nThrough the interplay of raga\, laya-taal\, and improvisation\, the performance traces how a shared musical language keeps discovering new shapes within familiar rules. Together\, they invite the audience to listen more closely\, to the movement of a raga\, the poetry of a bandish\, and the fine grain of a svara as it unfolds. This concert will be followed by a Music Appreciation Workshop\, extending the listening experience into a closer look at the language and aesthetics of Hindustani music. \nPushkar Lele will also conduct a 2 day Hindustani Music Appreciation workshop at BIC on Oct 3 and 4. More details here. \n\n\n\n\nSupported by:\n\n\nVenue: Seminar Halls\n\n\nA Vision of Sound\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSehQFD7cwDL-5VwXB2ElDgxLqJzPS6W7vbE-Z2WoI1QF7UCLA/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Performers*: Pushkar Lele\, Karthik Bhat\, Basavaraj Hiremath\n*Event Categories*: Music\, Performing Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/svara-darshan/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Music,Performing Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnail_SD.jpg
END:VEVENT
