UID:95443-1791129600-1791138600@bangaloreinternationalcentre.org
SUMMARY:Gudgudgudiya
DESCRIPTION:Gudgudgudiya is a slow\, restful workshop built around doll-making with everyday materials. Participants work with odds and ends\, forgotten scraps\, and overlooked objects\, letting imagination and touch lead the way. What might your hands remember once you stop directing them? \nRunning since the early days of the pandemic\, the workshop offers a quiet\, unhurried space to sit with a group and simply play with material\, no outcome required. It is especially suited to anyone who feels diffident about their creativity\, as well as anyone who wants company\, calm\, and the pleasure of making something with their hands. No prior experience or artistic confidence is needed. \nVenue: Library\n\n\nOdds\, Ends\, and Imagination\nFor All Ages (Children below 7 to Be Accompanied by an Adult)\nRSVPs will open Thu\, Oct 1 at 12 noon.\n*Facilitator*: Hansa Thapliyal\n*Event Categories*: Culture\, Heritage\, Workshops
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/gudgudgudiya/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Culture,Heritage,Workshops
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Thumbnail-15.jpg
